Experimental independent typed hook primitive

Original Go additions: SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0.

This test-only package adapts Event and Waterfall dispatch semantics of
@deepseek-ai/cordis 4.1.0, as modified and published by DeepSeek Harness.
Source-content pin: fcc0ad462172522aaf5c93a7b2e01f6b9f0b0159
https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/tree/fcc0ad462172522aaf5c93a7b2e01f6b9f0b0159
Reference file: vendor/cordis/src/events.ts (the preserved oracle copy is
 test/differential/oracle/vendor/cordis/src/events.ts).
Source package pin: @deepseek-ai/cordis 4.1.0, archive SHA-256
3b0099a6aa9b0b52c3e199042acf6f1ae195c5690f7de11aa61171bca7752eca.

Go adaptations/additions include typed event payloads and waterfall results,
explicit bail decisions, explicit scope audiences, ordered declared stages and
stable plugin-ID ordering, copy-on-write immutable atomic listener snapshots,
activation leases and lifecycle-owned cleanup, and an explicit already-started
future bridge. This package is an independent experiment, not the selected
kernel or a final SDK API. See README.md for semantic and integration gaps,
including raw source failure behavior versus canonical observer containment,
asynchronous waterfall representation, admission classes, ACTIVE ownership and
tenant-data definition checks. Unit tests are not a full corpus/S0 acceptance.

Both source notices are retained in full below. The Apache-2.0 terms on original
Go additions do not remove or replace the MIT terms on the adapted material.

